Hand-written plan in the shape postgres_fdw produces for EXPLAIN (VERBOSE, FORMAT JSON).
It was not captured from a server. It exists to exercise a label that core
PostgreSQL does not emit ("Remote SQL"), which holds a full query with literals.

-- foreign_scan_remote_sql.json --
[
  {
    "Plan": {
      "Node Type": "Foreign Scan",
      "Operation": "Select",
      "Parallel Aware": false,
      "Async Capable": false,
      "Relation Name": "accounts",
      "Schema": "public",
      "Alias": "a",
      "Startup Cost": 100.00,
      "Total Cost": 125.50,
      "Plan Rows": 2,
      "Plan Width": 36,
      "Output": ["id", "name"],
      "Remote SQL": "SELECT id, name FROM public.accounts WHERE ((status = 'active')) AND ((balance > 1000)) LIMIT 5"
    }
  }
]
